// ONE UPSTREAM HOLE, PATCHED FROM OUR SIDE: voxel cone tracing inside an SSR
// prepass, on a NORMAL-MAPPED material.
//
// CAUTION, AND THIS FILE PROVED IT TWICE: the Hlms parser does NOT respect //
// comments. An at-directive written inside a comment is still EXECUTED —
// quoting upstream's own source in this header produced a "piece already
// defined" error and an unmatched-block syntax error, from text that was
// nothing but explanation. Every directive named below is therefore spelled
// out in WORDS, never written with its at-sign. The same warning is at the top
// of JahFog_piece_vs_piece_ps.any, for the same reason.
//
// THE BUG, at the pin (ogre-next v3.0.0-783-g52d1a7aaf), reproduced the first
// time the SSR row was defaulted on at Epic — which is also the tier that turns
// VCT on, so this is not an exotic combination, it is THE combination:
//
//     ERROR: 0:2145: 'TBN' : undeclared identifier
//     Fragment Program …PixelShader_ps failed to compile
//
// and every normal-mapped object in the world renders as nothing.
//
// WHY IT HAPPENS. The piece "applyVoxelConeTracing"
// (Hlms/Pbs/Any/Vct_piece_ps.any:520-531) needs a tangent basis to rotate its
// diffuse cone directions with, and it declares a local TBN ITSELF — but only
// under a property test of "not normal_map". With a normal map it expects the
// TBN that the piece "LoadNormalData" builds
// (Hlms/Pbs/Any/Main/800.PixelShader_piece_ps.any:379-391) — and that insert
// sits inside a "not hlms_use_prepass" property block (:823-824), because in
// prepass mode the normal arrives from the G-buffer instead. So in a prepass
// pass, VCT references a variable that was never declared. Upstream never sees
// it: its SSR sample has no GI and its VCT samples have no prepass.
//
// (The no-normal-map half is fine under a prepass, and not by luck: PixelData
// #defines geomNormal to normal when there is no normal map (:48-52), so
// upstream's own declaration reads the G-buffer normal.)
//
// THE FIX, and why it is here rather than in a patch or a fork. Ogre-Next is
// patches-only, and this one does not need a patch: "custom_ps_posMaterialLoad"
// is a documented Hlms hook sitting immediately after the PixelData
// declaration (:798), in the same scope as the VCT block 1500 lines below, and
// it is unused everywhere else in this tree (the materials piece emitter uses
// custom_VStoPS, custom_ps_preLights, custom_ps_posExecution and
// custom_ps_uv_modifier_macros — src/modules/materials/core/pieceemitter.h).
// So we declare exactly what LoadNormalData would have declared, from the same
// interpolants, and upstream's code finds it.
//
// SCOPE, deliberately as narrow as the bug: the piece is only DEFINED when all
// three properties hold, so every other permutation's generated source is
// byte-for-byte what it was before this file existed (inserting an undefined
// piece emits nothing — which is how every custom_ hook works).
@property( vct_num_probes && hlms_use_prepass && normal_map )
@piece( custom_ps_posMaterialLoad )
	// Verbatim from LoadNormalData's tangent-basis block, minus the normal-map
	// sample itself (the prepass already did that; pixelData.normal comes from
	// the G-buffer). Upstream's "tbnApplyReflection" piece is NOT reused: it is
	// defined INSIDE the LoadNormalData body, which never expands here, so the
	// reflection term is written out under the same property test instead.
	pixelData.geomNormal = normalize( inPs.normal ) @insertpiece( two_sided_flip_normal );
	midf3 jahTangent = normalize( inPs.tangent );
	@property( hlms_qtangent || hlms_tangent4 )
		midf3 jahBinormal =
			normalize( cross( pixelData.geomNormal, jahTangent ) * inPs.biNormalReflection );
	@end
	@property( !hlms_qtangent && !hlms_tangent4 )
		midf3 jahBinormal = normalize( cross( pixelData.geomNormal, jahTangent ) );
	@end
	midf3x3 TBN = buildMidf3x3( jahTangent, jahBinormal, pixelData.geomNormal );
@end
@end
